(Bywaf Usage Guide) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Overview) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Bywaf is a Python 3 commandlet framework for authorized web application and) Tj
0 -11 Td
(network testing workflows. It presents a Metasploit-like interactive shell,) Tj
0 -11 Td
(loads commandlets from plugins, and connects commandlets through a SQLite-backed) Tj
0 -11 Td
(event bus.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(The core idea is simple: one commandlet discovers something and publishes it as) Tj
0 -11 Td
(an event; another commandlet consumes that event and publishes the next result.) Tj
0 -11 Td
(For example, hostscanner can publish live hosts, portscanner can consume) Tj
0 -11 Td
(those hosts and publish open ports, and HTTP commandlets can consume open ports) Tj
0 -11 Td
(and probe web services.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Use Bywaf only on systems and networks where you have explicit authorization.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Installation) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(During development, run Bywaf from the repository root:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    cd bywaf) Tj
0 -11 Td
(    python3 -m bywaf --help) Tj
0 -11 Td
(    python3 -m bywaf repl) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(For an editable local install:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    python3 -m pip install -e .) Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf --help) Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf repl) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(The project metadata defines a console script named bywaf, so packaged) Tj
0 -11 Td
(installations can expose Bywaf as a normal command instead of requiring) Tj
0 -11 Td
(python3 -m bywaf.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(The host and port scanner commandlets use nmap through a Python adapter. A) Tj
0 -11 Td
(local nmap binary is required for real scans. The adapter prefers nmaplib,) Tj
0 -11 Td
(then python-nmap, then nmapthon, then libnmap.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Starting Bywaf) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Start the interactive shell:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(or, from a source checkout:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    python3 -m bywaf) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Run one command non-interactively:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf run ls) Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf run cat README.md) Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf run 'hostscanner 127.0.0.1 | portscanner') Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Simple run commands do not need quotes. Use quotes when the command contains) Tj
0 -11 Td
(shell metacharacters such as |, &, >, or spaces that must be preserved) Tj
0 -11 Td
(inside a single argument.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(REPL Basics) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(The REPL prompt is:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
ET
