0 -11 Td
(Pipelines) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Pipelines connect commandlets with |:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf> hostscanner 127.0.0.1 | portscanner) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(The runner executes each stage in order. Events emitted by one stage are passed) Tj
0 -11 Td
(to the next stage as input. Events are also stored in SQLite with a pipeline ID) Tj
0 -11 Td
(and command run ID.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(This model allows downstream commandlets to consume only the output relevant to) Tj
0 -11 Td
(the current pipeline, rather than every historical event in the database.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Background Execution) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Append & to background a commandlet or pipeline:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf> hostscanner 192.168.0.1-255 &) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(Stage-level backgrounding works inside pipelines:) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(    bywaf> hostscanner 192.168.0.1-255 & | portscanner &) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
(In that example, portscanner listens for host.found rows created by the) Tj
0 -11 Td
(immediately upstream hostscanner run in the same pipeline. It does not consume) Tj
0 -11 Td
(unrelated host.found rows from older scans.) Tj
0 -11 Td
() Tj
0 -11 Td
